# Airbnb Clone Homepage - Product Requirements Document

## 1. Vision & Goal

The goal of the homepage is to attract visitors, build trust, and encourage them to explore available stays. It should have a modern, engaging design with animations and a "WOW" effect to make a strong first impression.

## 2. Scope

### ✅ In Scope (MVP)

- Hero section with catchy headline and background (image/video)
- Search bar with fields: Location, Check-in, Check-out, Guests
- Featured listings grid (3–6 cards with hover animations)
- Call-to-Action button(s) (e.g., "Start Your Journey")
- Responsive layout (desktop, tablet, mobile)
- Smooth animations/transitions

### ❌ Out of Scope (for now)

- Actual booking system
- User authentication
- Payments
- Backend database of listings

## 3. Functional Requirements

### Hero Section

- Full-width background (image or video)
- Animated headline + subtext
- CTA button with hover effect

### Search Bar

- Inputs for location, dates, guests
- Subtle animation when focused
- Responsive collapse into mobile-friendly format

### Featured Listings

- Grid with cards (image, title, price, location)
- Hover animations (scale, shadow, subtle motion)
- Clickable (placeholder links)

### Footer

- Basic footer with brand + navigation links

## 4. Non-Functional Requirements

- **Performance**: Initial page load under 2s on a standard 4G network
- **Accessibility**: WCAG 2.1 AA compliance (alt text, ARIA labels)
- **Responsive Design**: Works seamlessly on desktop, tablet, and mobile
- **Animations**: Smooth (60fps) with no jank
- **SEO Friendly**: Meta tags, OpenGraph, semantic HTML

## 5. Architecture Outline

### Tech Stack

- **Frontend Framework**: Next.js (React + SSR/SSG support)
- **Styling**: TailwindCSS
- **Animations**: Framer Motion
- **UI Components**: shadcn/ui (for consistent UI kit)
- **Linting & Formatting**: ESLint + Prettier
- **Version Control**: Git (GitHub)
- **Deployment**: Vercel

## 6. Development Guidelines

- Follow modern React patterns and hooks
- Implement responsive design with mobile-first approach
- Ensure smooth animations with proper performance optimization
- Maintain consistent UI/UX patterns using shadcn/ui components
- Write clean, maintainable code with proper TypeScript types
- Follow accessibility best practices throughout development
